  "title": "Amber Y FDE 4256 NDE 4256",
  "date": "11-18-2009",
  "content": "It all started seconds before the crash occurred I got this really scared feeling then a feeling of complete peace, like everything was going to be alright. For an instant, time stood still. I had my four children with me; Autumn, five years old; Summer, two years old; James, eighteen months old; and Brandon, three months old. I was scared to death for them. If it was not for the children needing me, I could have just let that feeling of calm and love take me away. Then I came back right when my van got smashed by the other car. I remember some lady pulling my oldest daughter from the car. Then I got out of the car. I was pretty shook up. But when I saw my kids were okay, I was fine. I don't know why I didn't die, my van was totaled the whole front end on the driver's side smashed in. I am just glad, you know something told me that day to make my daughter Autumn sit in the back and I am so glad she did because the air bag popped out on that side first and she probably would have died.",
